genvalues of a Schr\\\"odinger operator (and the Laplacian, in particular). For horoconvex domains in hyperbolic space, Nguyen, Stancu and Wei conjectured that it is possible to obtain a lower bound on the fundamental gap in terms of the diameter of the domain and the dimension [IMRN2022]. In this article, we prove this conjecture by establishing conformal log-concavity estimates for the first eigenfunction. This builds off earlier work by the authors and Saha as well as recent work by Cho, Wei and Yang. We also prove spectral gap estimates for a more general class of problems on conformally flat manifolds and investigate the relationship between the gap and the inradius. For example, we establish gap estimates for domains in $\\mathbb{S}^1 \\times \\mathbb{S}^{N-1}$ which are convex with respect to the universal affine cover--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUpward flagness for linear subdiagrams with a heavy edge (type B-style conjecture) (https://api.emergentmind.com/open-problems/upward-flagness-linear-heavy-edge)\nciteturn5search1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 4 months ago; # Upward flagness for linear subdiagrams with a heavy edge (type B-style conjecture)\n\nProve that for any irreducible spherical Artin group A_Λ and any linear subdiagram Λ'⊂Λ with consecutive vertices {s_i}_{i=1}^n such that the edge between s_{n−1} and s_n has label at least 4, the vertex set of the relative Artin complex Δ_{Λ,Λ'} endowed with the order induced by s_1<⋯<s_n forms a bowtie-free, upward flag poset.\n\n# Upward flagness for linear subdiagrams with a heavy edge (type B-style conjecture)\n\nProve that for any irreducible spherical Artin group A_Λ and any linear subdiagram Λ'⊂Λ with consecutive vertices {s_i}_{i=1}^n such that the edge between s_{n−1} and s_n has label at least 4, the vertex set of the relative Artin complex Δ_{Λ,Λ'} endowed with the order induced by s_1<⋯<s_n forms a bowtie-free, upward flag poset.\n\n### Background\n\nThis conjecture formulates a key link condition needed to apply Haettel’s contractibility criteria to cores. It asserts a strong combinatorial property (bowtie-free and upward flag) for the ordered vertex set of Δ_{Λ,Λ'} in the spherical base case, when a terminal edge has label ≥4 (capturing B-type features).\n\nThe bowtie-free part is already known from prior work, but the upward flagness remains open in general; it is verified in several special cases (e.g., type B_n) within the paper.\n\n### References\n\nConjecture. Suppose $A_S$ is an irreducible spherical Artin group with Coxeter diagram $\\Lambda$. Let $\\Lambda'$ be a linear subdiagram of $\\Lambda$ with consecutive vertices ${s_i}{i=1}^{n$} such that the edge between $s{n-1}$ and $s_n$ has label $\\ge 4$. Then the vertex set of $\\Delta_{\\Lambda,\\Lambda'}$ equipped with the relation induced from $s_1<s_2<\\cdots<s_n$ (as in Definition~\\ref{def:order}) is a bowtie free and upward flag poset.\n\n— Cycles in spherical Deligne complexes and application to $K(π,1)$-conjecture for Artin groups  (2405.12068 - Huang, 2024) in Section 2.6 (Link conditions at the base case), Conjecture 2.4\n\n### Related Problems\n\n1.\n\nContractibility of cores (relative Artin complexes for almost spherical subsets)  Same Paper\n\n2.\n\nContractibility of Δ_{S,S'} via a convex geodesic bicombing metric for non-exceptional types  Same Paper\n\n3.\n\nCAT(0) metric for exceptional almost spherical types  Same Paper\n\n4.\n\nDownward flagness after (b1,b2)-subdivision for type D_n subdiagrams  Same Paper\n\n5.\n\nArbitrary intersection of parabolic subgroups in general Artin groups  2402.10919\n\n6.\n\nIsomorphism between the extended Artin group and the extended Seidel–Thomas braid group  2411.03092\n\n7.\n\nHomology preservation in Λ(Δ), the induced subcomplex on all vertices with nontrivial link homology  2401.05962\n\n8.\n\nCharacterize When the Noncrossing Partition Poset is a Lattice in Rank ≥ 4  2509.00445\n\n9.\n\nKashiwa